sed imperative methods instead for component-level behavior.",[14,1638,1640],{"id":1639},"options-api-equivalent","Options API Equivalent",[19,1642,1643],{},"Directive registration and hook definitions are identical in the Options API — the only difference is where local, component-scoped directives are declared:",[32,1645,1646],{"language":34},[37,1647,1649],{"className":39,"code":1648,"language":34,"meta":41,"style":41},"\u003Cscript>\nexport default {\n  directives: {\n    focus: {\n      mounted: (el) => el.focus()\n    }\n  }\n}\n\u003C\u002Fscript>\n\n\u003Ctemplate>\n  \u003Cinput v-focus \u002F>\n\u003C\u002Ftemplate>\n",[43,1650,1651,1659,1668,1673,1678,1697,1701,1705,1709,1717,1721,1729,1739],{"__ignoreMap":41},[46,1652,1653,1655,1657],{"class":48,"line":49},[46,1654,53],{"class":52},[46,1656,57],{"class":56},[46,1658,64],{"class":52},[46,1660,1661,1663,1666],{"class":48,"line":67},[46,1662,420],{"class":83},[46,1664,1665],{"class":83}," default",[46,1667,94],{"class":52},[46,1669,1670],{"class":48,"line":74},[46,1671,1672],{"class":52},"  directives: {\n",[46,1674,1675],{"class":48,"line":80},[46,1676,1677],{"class":52},"    focus: {\n",[46,1679,1680,1683,1685,1687,1689,1691,1693,1695],{"class":48,"line":97},[46,1681,1682],{"class":60},"      mounted",[46,1684,103],{"class":52},[46,1686,107],{"class":106},[46,1688,110],{"class":52},[46,1690,113],{"class":83},[46,1692,116],{"class":52},[46,1694,119],{"class":60},[46,1696,122],{"class":52},[46,1698,1699],{"class":48,"line":125},[46,1700,762],{"class":52},[46,1702,1703],{"class":48,"line":131},[46,1704,505],{"class":52},[46,1706,1707],{"class":48,"line":141},[46,1708,128],{"class":52},[46,1710,1711,1713,1715],{"class":48,"line":148},[46,1712,134],{"class":52},[46,1714,57],{"class":56},[46,1716,64],{"class":52},[46,1718,1719],{"class":48,"line":158},[46,1720,145],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":144},[46,1722,1723,1725,1727],{"class":48,"line":183},[46,1724,53],{"class":52},[46,1726,153],{"class":56},[46,1728,64],{"class":52},[46,1730,1731,1733,1735,1737],{"class":48,"line":803},[46,1732,161],{"class":52},[46,1734,164],{"class":56},[46,1736,167],{"class":60},[46,1738,180],{"class":52},[46,1740,1741,1743,1745],{"class":48,"line":809},[46,1742,134],{"class":52},[46,1744,153],{"class":56},[46,1746,64],{"class":52},[14,1748,1750],{"id":1749},"tips-tricks","💡 Tips & Tricks",[987,1752,1753,1759,1778,1798,1815],{},[1005,1754,1755,1758],{},[23,1756,1757],{},"Idiom"," — Reach for a directive only when the behavior needs direct DOM access with no natural component\u002Fprop shape — most \"I need reusable logic\" needs are better served by a composable; directives are the minority case, not the default reuse mechanism.",[1005,1760,1761,1764,1765,1767,1768,441,1771,1774,1775,1777],{},[23,1762,1763],{},"Debug"," — Store any handler\u002Felement reference a directive creates directly on the ",[43,1766,107],{}," itself (",[43,1769,1770],{},"el._myHandler",[43,1772,1773],{},"el._myTooltip",") — it's the simplest reliable way to retrieve the exact same reference later in ",[43,1776,404],{}," for correct cleanup, without a separate WeakMap or module-level registry.",[1005,1779,1780,1782,1783,1786,1787,1518,1789,1791,1792,1794,1795,1797],{},[23,1781,1757],{}," — Prefer the function shorthand (",[43,1784,1785],{},"{mounted, updated}"," combined) whenever a directive's ",[43,1788,364],{},[43,1790,384],{}," logic are identical — it removes a whole category of \"I updated ",[43,1793,364],{}," but forgot to update ",[43,1796,384],{}," to match\" bugs.",[1005,1799,1800,1802,1803,1806,1807,521,1809,1811,1812,1814],{},[23,1801,1763],{}," — ",[43,1804,1805],{},"binding.oldValue"," (available in ",[43,1808,384],{},[43,1810,374],{},") lets a directive skip redundant DOM work when the bound value hasn't actually changed in a way that matters — useful when a directive's ",[43,1813,384],{}," hook would otherwise run expensive work on every unrelated re-render of the host component.",[1005,1816,1817,1820,1821,1823,1824,1827,1828,1830,1831,1833],{},[23,1818,1819],{},"Performance"," — A ",[43,1822,665],{},"-style directive should register its listener on ",[43,1825,1826],{},"document"," once per element (with cleanup in ",[43,1829,404],{},"), never inside a per-render hook — registering inside ",[43,1832,384],{}," without matching removal accumulates duplicate listeners on every re-render.",[14,1835,1837],{"id":1836},"️-edge-cases-gotchas","⚠️ Edge Cases & Gotchas",[987,1839,1840,1846,1873,1897,1919],{},[1005,1841,1842,1845],{},[23,1843,1844],{},"Applying a DOM-manipulation directive to a component only ever touches its single root element"," — And only works predictably if the component happens to render a single root node; a component using multiple root nodes (a \"fragment\" component) makes directive application ambiguous, and Vue warns rather than guessing which node you meant.",[1005,1847,1848,1853,1854,1856,1857,1859,1860,1862,1863,1866,1867,1869,1870,1872],{},[23,1849,1850,1852],{},[43,1851,832],{}," silently does nothing if given a different function reference than the one originally added"," — An inline arrow function passed to ",[43,1855,792],{}," inside ",[43,1858,364],{}," cannot be removed in ",[43,1861,404],{}," unless the ",[1069,1864,1865],{},"exact same"," function reference was saved somewhere (typically on ",[43,1868,107],{}," itself) — passing a new inline arrow function to ",[43,1871,832],{}," compiles fine, runs without error, and simply fails to remove anything, leaking the original listener.",[1005,1874,1875,1881,1882,1885,1886,1888,1889,1892,1893,1896],{},[23,1876,1877,1878,1880],{},"A ",[43,1879,665],{}," directive added without a delay\u002FsetTimeout can immediately fire on the very click that opened the element"," — Because the same synchronous click event that toggles ",[43,1883,1884],{},"isOpen = true"," also bubbles up to ",[43,1887,1826],{}," in the current event loop tick if the listener is attached in the same tick — attaching via ",[43,1890,1891],{},"setTimeout(() => ..., 0)"," (or listening on ",[43,1894,1895],{},"click"," in the capture phase with care) defers registration to the next tick, avoiding the self-closing bug.",[1005,1898,1899,1904,1905,1908,1909,1911,1912,1915,1916,1918],{},[23,1900,1901,1903],{},[43,1902,384],{}," on a directive fires on every re-render of the containing component, not just when the directive's own bound value changes"," — Exactly like a component's ",[43,1906,1907],{},"onUpdated"," hook (chapter 08), a directive's ",[43,1910,384],{}," hook can fire far more often than \"the value I actually care about changed\" — compare ",[43,1913,1914],{},"binding.value"," against ",[43,1917,1805],{}," explicitly if the hook does anything non-trivial.",[1005,1920,1921,1927,1928,1930],{},[23,1922,1923,1924,1926],{},"A directive that appends a DOM node outside the component tree (like the tooltip example) will leak that node forever if ",[43,1925,404],{}," cleanup is skipped or throws"," — Because that node lives outside Vue's own tracked template tree, Vue's own unmounting process has no idea it exists and cannot clean it up on your behalf under any circumstance — this responsibility belongs entirely and exclusively to the directive's own ",[43,1929,404],{}," hook.",[14,1932,1934],{"id":1933},"spot-the-bug","🧠 Spot the Bug",[19,1936,1877,1937,1940],{},[43,1938,1939],{},"v-highlight"," directive is meant to update an element's background color whenever the bound value changes, but after the first render it never updates again.",[32,1942,1943],{"language":195,"filename":410},[37,1944,1946],{"className":199,"code":1945,"language":195,"meta":41,"style":41},"export const vHighlight = {\n  mounted(el, binding) {\n    el.style.backgroundColor = binding.value\n  }\n}\n",[43,1947,1948,1960,1974,1982,1986],{"__ignoreMap":41},[46,1949,1950,1952,1954,1956,1958],{"class":48,"line":49},[46,1951,420],{"class":83},[46,1953,423],{"class":83},[46,1955,426],{"class":87},[46,1957,91],{"class":83},[46,1